---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
import Portrait from '../components/Portrait.astro';
import { site, timeline } from '../data/site';
---
<Base title="About" description="IB6 is led by Illia Bovkun, who built his first online store at 17. Experience across oil & gas, venture capital and startups, now focused on AI automation for growing businesses.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container founder">
      <div class="reveal"><Portrait alt="Portrait of Illia Bovkun" eager /></div>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow reveal">About IB6</p>
        <h1 class="display reveal" style="font-size:clamp(44px,5.6vw,76px)">Illia Bovkun</h1>
        <p class="lead reveal" style="margin-top:20px">
          Founder of IB6. Building on the web since 17 — with experience across oil & gas, venture capital
          and startups. Today, my team and I help growing businesses run on AI.
        </p>
        <p class="reveal" style="margin-top:28px;display:flex;gap:28px;flex-wrap:wrap">
          <a class="link-arrow" href={site.booking}>Book a call →</a>
          <a class="link-arrow" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
          {site.linkedin && <a class="link-arrow" href={site.linkedin} rel="noopener">LinkedIn →</a>}
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="container">
      <ol class="timeline reveal">
        {timeline.map((t) => (
          <li><span class="t-label">{t.label}</span><span class="t-title">{t.title}</span><span class="t-body">{t.body}</span></li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="prose reveal">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0">It started with one online store</h2>
        <p>
          At 17 I built my first website: an online shop, made from scratch. With no budget for ads, the only
          way to get customers was search — so I learned SEO by doing it. The shop became a successful business
          and ran for years. It taught me the lesson I still work by: technology only matters when it brings in
          customers or saves real time.
        </p>
        <h2>Three very different schools</h2>
        <p>
          In oil & gas I saw how much value organisations lose to manual processes and slow reporting. In venture
          capital I learned to look at a business like an investor — what really drives its value, and what is
          noise. With startups I learned to ship: small teams, short runways, no room for slideware.
        </p>
        <h2>Why IB6 exists</h2>
        <p>
          AI has made automation affordable for businesses that could never justify an enterprise IT project.
          But most of them are stuck between tools that never connect and advice that never gets built. IB6
          closes that gap: we find where AI pays off, build it, and make sure customers can find you — in Google
          and in AI answers.
        </p>
        <h2>Why “IB6”?</h2>
        <p>
          It’s my initials — I.B. — and the six letters of my surname, Bovkun. A reminder that behind every
          project there’s a person who answers for it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Cta title="Let’s see if we’re a fit." />
</Base>
